1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,259
February of 2015.

2
00:00:04,140 --> 00:00:05,879
A beach on the coast of Libya.

3
00:00:06,639 --> 00:00:11,480
Twenty-one men in a line, and every one of them had a chance to walk away.

4
00:00:12,199 --> 00:00:16,780
Twenty of them were Egyptian Christians, most of them from the same few villages.

5
00:00:17,480 --> 00:00:21,719
The twenty-first man wasn't from their country, and he wasn't from their church.

6
00:00:22,420 --> 00:00:25,660
Some say he wasn't even a believer when he first got there.

7
00:00:26,059 --> 00:00:32,060
And what he said at the very end is still being talked about, eleven years later.

8
00:00:32,060 --> 00:00:35,280
This is a true story, and I'm going to tell it to you straight.

9
00:00:35,859 --> 00:00:38,299
I won't show you what those men saw on that beach.

10
00:00:38,840 --> 00:00:39,880
You don't need to see it.

11
00:00:40,320 --> 00:00:42,640
What you need is what they did with it.

12
00:00:48,804 --> 00:00:52,824
Most of them came from Minya, Egypt, farm country along the Nile.

13
00:00:53,484 --> 00:00:56,704
Thirteen of them came from one little village called al-Our.

14
00:00:57,404 --> 00:01:06,264
Sugarcane and clover, dirt lanes, donkey carts, and houses built one floor at a time, because one floor is all anybody could pay for that year.

15
00:01:06,804 --> 00:01:07,824
There wasn't much work.

16
00:01:08,304 --> 00:01:11,544
So the young men did what poor men everywhere have always done.

17
00:01:11,904 --> 00:01:17,364
They went where the work was, and for a lot of Egyptian laborers back then, the work was in Libya.

18
00:01:18,144 --> 00:01:19,304
Girgis was twenty-four.

19
00:01:19,984 --> 00:01:25,124
He was engaged, planning a wedding for that August, and he meant to come home for good after it.

20
00:01:25,624 --> 00:01:30,664
Loka was twenty-seven, a husband and a father, sending his pay home to feed his kids.

21
00:01:31,304 --> 00:01:34,104
Two of the men, Bishoy and Samuel, were brothers.

22
00:01:34,604 --> 00:01:38,884
A lot of Coptic Christians tattoo a small cross on the inside of the right wrist.

23
00:01:39,224 --> 00:01:42,704
In some places over there, that little cross can cost you a job.

24
00:01:42,704 --> 00:01:46,564
They wear it anyway, so everybody knows whose they are.

25
00:01:48,248 --> 00:01:52,228
In the city of Sirte, on the Libyan coast, they worked construction.

26
00:01:52,948 --> 00:01:59,868
They slept on mattresses in shared rooms, cooked on gas burners, sent the money home, and prayed together at night.

27
00:02:00,608 --> 00:02:03,928
And working right beside them was a young man from West Africa.

28
00:02:04,488 --> 00:02:07,708
Most accounts say he came from Ghana, and a few say Chad.

29
00:02:08,228 --> 00:02:11,408
He was a migrant worker like the rest of them, chasing a paycheck.

30
00:02:12,188 --> 00:02:14,588
History knows him as Matthew Ayariga.

31
00:02:15,268 --> 00:02:17,468
Honestly, we don't know a lot about him.

32
00:02:17,468 --> 00:02:19,668
Some say he was already a Christian.

33
00:02:20,128 --> 00:02:23,688
Others say he came to faith by watching how those Egyptian men lived.

34
00:02:24,248 --> 00:02:27,348
Either way, he was the one who didn't fit in that group.

35
00:02:27,908 --> 00:02:31,568
Different country, different language, and no cross on his wrist.

36
00:02:33,455 --> 00:02:38,815
Around the turn of the new year, armed men from ISIS came through the worker housing in Sirte.

37
00:02:39,315 --> 00:02:40,755
They sorted people out.

38
00:02:41,295 --> 00:02:42,435
The Muslims could go.

39
00:02:42,975 --> 00:02:44,475
The Christians they took.

40
00:02:45,175 --> 00:02:48,175
They took the Egyptians, and they took Matthew.

41
00:02:48,975 --> 00:02:53,935
Back home in Minya, the families got the news, and then they got nothing.

42
00:02:54,735 --> 00:02:55,495
Weeks of it.

43
00:02:56,015 --> 00:03:03,315
Mothers in black headscarves walking to the church every night, fathers staring at the phone, and nobody knowing a thing.

44
00:03:05,053 --> 00:03:08,393
On February fifteenth, ISIS put out a video.

45
00:03:08,993 --> 00:03:11,693
They called it a message to the nation of the cross.

46
00:03:12,373 --> 00:03:16,173
They meant for it to scare every Christian on earth into keeping quiet.

47
00:03:16,773 --> 00:03:19,173
What they didn't count on was those men.

48
00:03:19,733 --> 00:03:24,313
Right up to the end, every one of them could have said what their captors wanted and lived.

49
00:03:24,673 --> 00:03:28,453
And by most accounts, a lot of them were praying out loud instead.

50
00:03:28,943 --> 00:03:30,433
Ya Rabbi Yasou.

51
00:03:30,433 --> 00:03:32,933
It means, oh my Lord Jesus.

52
00:03:33,753 --> 00:03:38,313
And Matthew, the one who wasn't from their church, was asked about his faith.

53
00:03:38,893 --> 00:03:42,353
The answer that's been told around the world ever since is this.

54
00:03:43,013 --> 00:03:44,933
Their God is my God.

55
00:03:45,713 --> 00:03:47,193
He didn't grow up in their church.

56
00:03:47,673 --> 00:03:49,013
He didn't speak their language.

57
00:03:49,553 --> 00:03:54,153
He watched how they lived, and when it counted the most, he picked their God.

58
00:03:55,928 --> 00:03:58,788
There's a woman in the Bible who made that same choice.

59
00:03:59,328 --> 00:04:00,548
Her name was Ruth.

60
00:04:01,188 --> 00:04:02,468
She wasn't an Israelite.

61
00:04:02,888 --> 00:04:09,728
She was a foreigner from Moab, and when she was told to go back to her own people and her own gods, she said this.

62
00:04:10,368 --> 00:04:12,448
Ruth chapter one, verse sixteen.

63
00:04:12,968 --> 00:04:28,648
And Ruth said, Intreat me not to leave thee, or to return from following after thee: for whither thou goest, I will go; and where thou lodgest, I will lodge: thy people shall be my people, and thy God my God:

64
00:04:29,368 --> 00:04:32,868
Three thousand years apart, and almost the same words.

65
00:04:33,548 --> 00:04:36,608
There's one more Scripture that fits this man like a glove.

66
00:04:37,208 --> 00:04:42,508
Jesus told a story about a man who owned a vineyard and kept hiring laborers all day long.

67
00:04:42,908 --> 00:04:45,648
Early in the morning, then at nine, then at noon.

68
00:04:45,988 --> 00:04:51,628
And at the very last hour of the workday, the eleventh hour, he went out and hired a few more.

69
00:04:51,628 --> 00:04:54,368
When it came time to pay, look what happened.

70
00:04:54,888 --> 00:04:56,888
Matthew chapter twenty, verse nine.

71
00:04:57,448 --> 00:05:02,728
And when they came that were hired about the eleventh hour, they received every man a penny.

72
00:05:03,548 --> 00:05:06,888
Those men on the beach were laborers, every one of them.

73
00:05:07,228 --> 00:05:09,288
And Matthew was the last one hired.

74
00:05:09,748 --> 00:05:13,148
He got the same reward as the men who'd been working since sunup.

75
00:05:13,628 --> 00:05:16,728
That's grace, and that's how our God pays.

76
00:05:18,491 --> 00:05:20,471
Now here's the part that got me.

77
00:05:21,051 --> 00:05:29,991
A few days after the video came out, Bishoy and Samuel's brother, Beshir Kamel, went on a Christian TV channel called SAT-7, live.

78
00:05:30,831 --> 00:05:32,291
And he thanked ISIS.

79
00:05:32,991 --> 00:05:39,351
He thanked them for leaving in the part where his brothers called on Jesus, because hearing it made his own faith stronger.

80
00:05:40,011 --> 00:05:43,251
Then he prayed for the killers, right there on the air.

81
00:05:43,651 --> 00:05:46,751
He asked God to open their eyes so they could be saved.

82
00:05:46,751 --> 00:05:55,071
He said if his mother ever met the man who killed her son, she would invite him into her home, and ask God to open his eyes too.

83
00:05:55,751 --> 00:06:01,551
Another mother, whose son Milad was one of the twenty-one, said she was thankful he died for the cross.

84
00:06:01,931 --> 00:06:10,491
And a father named Samir, who lost his son Girgis, the young man with the wedding planned, said he forgave them, and he prays they'll see the truth.

85
00:06:11,251 --> 00:06:14,291
Nobody in those villages went on TV cursing anybody.

86
00:06:14,791 --> 00:06:15,491
They forgave.

87
00:06:15,491 --> 00:06:17,931
People don't do that on their own strength.

88
00:06:18,371 --> 00:06:20,431
That's Jesus living inside somebody.

89
00:06:22,167 --> 00:06:27,987
The men who killed them buried them in a mass grave with no names, out on the coast near Sirte.

90
00:06:28,527 --> 00:06:31,047
In 2017 the grave was found.

91
00:06:31,327 --> 00:06:37,647
And in May of 2018, they were flown home to Egypt, and a church was built in al-Our to hold them.

92
00:06:38,287 --> 00:06:42,527
Within a week of their deaths, the Coptic Church had already named them saints.

93
00:06:43,227 --> 00:06:48,107
In 2023, the Catholic Church added them to its own list of martyrs.

94
00:06:48,247 --> 00:06:54,647
Two churches that have been split for more than fifteen hundred years, agreeing on twenty-one working men.

95
00:06:55,247 --> 00:06:57,467
And ISIS really didn't plan on this part.

96
00:06:57,887 --> 00:07:00,327
That video was supposed to make Christians go quiet.

97
00:07:00,927 --> 00:07:10,207
Instead, the story of these men has been told in churches, books, songs and films all over the world, and there's a feature film about them planned for this year.

98
00:07:11,841 --> 00:07:16,121
Jesus put it plain in the book of Matthew, chapter ten, verse thirty-two.

99
00:07:16,821 --> 00:07:23,881
Whosoever therefore shall confess me before men, him will I confess also before my Father which is in heaven.

100
00:07:24,661 --> 00:07:27,621
Twenty of those men had known Jesus their whole lives.

101
00:07:28,201 --> 00:07:31,301
One of them met Him, at least in part, by watching them.

102
00:07:31,721 --> 00:07:32,901
So let me ask you something.

103
00:07:33,481 --> 00:07:34,461
Who's watching you?

104
00:07:34,921 --> 00:07:36,141
Because somebody is.

105
00:07:36,561 --> 00:07:37,221
Your kids.

106
00:07:37,681 --> 00:07:39,361
The man at the next machine at work.

107
00:07:39,361 --> 00:07:43,161
The cousin who never goes to church but notices whether you do.

108
00:07:43,521 --> 00:07:49,041
They're watching how you handle a bad day, a bill you can't pay, and a man who did you wrong.

109
00:07:49,441 --> 00:07:53,021
And if you've never given your life to Jesus, you don't need a beach.

110
00:07:53,381 --> 00:07:56,581
You just need to tell Him, tonight, in your own words.

111
00:07:57,121 --> 00:07:59,061
He will meet you right where you are.

112
00:07:59,501 --> 00:08:01,781
If you want to, pray this with me.

113
00:08:02,301 --> 00:08:05,961
Lord Jesus, I've been watching from the outside long enough.

114
00:08:06,401 --> 00:08:09,021
I believe you died for me and rose again.

115
00:08:09,361 --> 00:08:10,221
Forgive me.

116
00:08:10,721 --> 00:08:12,341
I want you to be my God.

117
00:08:12,921 --> 00:08:17,381
Take my life, and help me live it so somebody else can see you in me.

118
00:08:17,861 --> 00:08:19,681
In Jesus' name, amen.

119
00:08:20,501 --> 00:08:22,781
If that was your prayer, type amen below.

120
00:08:23,341 --> 00:08:26,281
And next time, a story most people have never heard.

121
00:08:26,741 --> 00:08:32,041
A frozen pond in Holland, back in fifteen sixty-nine, and a man who turned around.
